 2027\, Barcelona (EUR 2\,000 honorarium\, EUR 2\,000 production fund\, tra
 vel and accommodation)
DESCRIPTION:Closes 31 Jan 2027 at 23:59 CET.\n\nSant Andreu Contemporani\, 
 with Fabra i Coats\, invites one international curator to Barcelona to sit
  on the jury of the Miquel Casablancas Prize for the Visual Arts 2027 and 
 then build a curatorial project with four Catalan artists\, or artists lin
 ked to the Catalan context\, chosen from the prize's applicants.\n\nOrgani
 sation: Sant Andreu Contemporani\, with Fabra i Coats - Fàbrica de Creaci
 ó de Barcelona\nLocation: Fabra i Coats\, Sant Andreu\, Barcelona\, Spain
 . Open to international curators\; proposals limited to Europe\, the Medit
 erranean and North Africa.\nAward: EUR 2\,000 curator honorarium\, EUR 2\,
 000 exhibition production fund and EUR 700 for travel and expenses (all su
 bject to tax)\, plus accommodation and a workspace. Each selected artist i
 s paid EUR 500. No application fee mentioned.\nDuration: One month in resi
 dence in Barcelona in April 2027 (extendable by a month without extra pay)
 \; exhibition abroad during one month between 15 September and 10 December
  2027\n\nMore: https://santandreucontemporani.org/convocatories/open-call-
 sac-international-curatorial-residency-program-2027-2/?utm_source=artifici
